# ShopNest Backend

Boilerplate backend for ShopNest — Node.js · Express.js · TypeScript · MongoDB · Mongoose · Zod · CORS

Auth is handled by **Better Auth** on the frontend. This backend only *verifies*
credentials (see `src/middlewares/authenticate.middleware.ts`).

## Getting Started

```bash
npm install
cp .env.example .env
# fill in MONGODB_URI, CLIENT_URL, GEMINI_API_KEY, etc.
npm run dev
```

Server runs at `http://localhost:5000/api/v1` by default.
Health check: `GET /api/v1/health`

## Scripts

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `npm run dev` | Start dev server with nodemon + ts-node |
| `npm run build` | Compile TypeScript to `dist/` |
| `npm start` | Run compiled server from `dist/` |
| `npm run lint` | Lint `src/` |
| `npm run format` | Format `src/` with Prettier |

## Adding a New Module

```
src/modules/<name>/
  <name>.model.ts       ← Mongoose schema
  <name>.types.ts        ← TypeScript types
  <name>.schema.ts       ← Zod validation schemas
  <name>.service.ts      ← Business logic
  <name>.controller.ts   ← Thin request handlers
  <name>.routes.ts       ← Route definitions
```

Then register it in `src/routes/index.ts`:

```ts
import productRoutes from "../modules/products/product.routes";
apiRouter.use("/products", productRoutes);
```

That's it — no other shared files need to be touched, so multiple developers
can work on separate modules without merge conflicts.

## Do NOT Build Yet

- Login / Register / Logout (Better Auth handles this on the frontend)
- Custom JWT system
- Full Users / Products / Cart / Wishlist / Orders modules (assigned separately)
- Rate limiting, Redis, Kafka, Docker (not decided yet)
- Real Gemini integration (plug into `ai.service.ts` when ready)

## Request Flow

```
Request → Route → authenticate (if needed) → authorize (if needed)
        → validate(zodSchema) (if needed) → Controller (asyncHandler)
        → Service (business logic) → Model → MongoDB
```

## Response Format

**Success**

```json
{ "success": true, "message": "Operation successful", "data": {} }
```

**Error**

```json
{ "success": false, "message": "Something went wrong" }
```
